atings are split, with several calling the race a Tossup and others Lean D or Likely D, averaging out to a tilt toward Democrats. Prediction markets price Moskowitz near 70 percent. Polling is sparse and dated, with a May survey showing Moskowitz up ten. The race has centered on cost of living, antisemitism, school safety, and views of Trump. The forecast gives Moskowitz a modest edge, with meaningful uncertainty given the district's Republican lean and heavy outside spending.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7798, "margin": 4.68}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7278, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7527, "margin": 4.0}]}